  <!-- browse page -->
  <data name="Browse_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Browse the Templates</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Intro_1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Every template is a stand-alone HTML page. Open one to read it, or</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Intro_DownloadLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>download the whole set</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Intro_2" xml:space="preserve"><value>and copy the templates folder into your project. Yellow TODO and TIP boxes are instructions for you to delete, text in ALL CAPS is to be replaced, and example text carries a coloured rule on its right-hand edge. The</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Intro_FaqLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>FAQ</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Intro_3" xml:space="preserve"><value>explains the conventions in detail.</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Intro_Groupings" xml:space="preserve"><value>The same templates are listed three ways below; pick whichever suits how you think about a project. Indented entries are worksheets attached to the document above them.</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_ByActivity" xml:space="preserve"><value>By activity</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_BySequence" xml:space="preserve"><value>By suggested sequence</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_All" xml:space="preserve"><value>All templates, alphabetically</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Getting the templates</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_DownloadLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>Download the template archive</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_1" xml:space="preserve"><value>as a zip, or clone</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_RepoLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>the repository</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_1b" xml:space="preserve"><value>The templates live in the templates folder and need nothing but a browser.</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_2a" xml:space="preserve"><value>Read the recommended</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_2b" xml:space="preserve"><value>before editing, and</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_UpgradeLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>how to upgrade</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_2c" xml:space="preserve"><value>if you have documents made from an earlier release.</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_3a" xml:space="preserve"><value>The original project's words of wisdom, background essays linked from each template, are preserved in the</value></data>
  <data name="Browse_Getting_ArchiveLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>Internet Archive</value></data>
